      "content": "It sounds like you're dealing with a more profound sense of dislocation and loss. It's a really tough feeling to accept when everything you once knew and loved has changed beyond recognition. Your words feel like a honest expression of feelings of irrelevance and disconnection, and it's okay to acknowledge and accept those emotions. Sometimes, taking a step back from trying to put yourself together can be a necessary part of the healing process, and allowing yourself to rest in this uncertainty can be a form of acceptance.",
